{{Faction | faction = Prolongers | image1 = | caption-image1 = | nickname = Cheaters | philosophy = Life is the only point to living. | founded = | factol = | sigilhq = | homefield = [[Ysgard]] | allies = [[Fated]], [[Doomguard]], [[Xaositects]] | enemies = [[Fraternity of Order]], [[Harmonium]], [[Mercykillers]] | predecessor = | successor = }}
The '''Prolongers''' aren't really a sect, although they're often seen as one by others who are aware of them<ref name="pwhb56">{{b|Planescape|The Planewalker's Handbook|pdf=17280|nip=1|page=56}}</ref>. They're a secret brotherhood of people who believe life is the only point to living. Or, depending on who you ask, are absolutely terrified of death.
Through a secretive process, a Prolonger's body is changed so they can drain the life force from others, similar to the undead, in order to help bolster their own lives.
== History ==
== Philosophy ==
== Role ==
== Membership == : ''See also:'' [[List of Prolongers members]]
Although open to anyone, the vast majority of Prolongers are human; apparently the terror of mortality runs deep in humans. Prolongers' eyes become cold and dead, as they cannot hide the age of their spirits. They're easy to startle, and always uncomfortable, due to living in a state of perpetual paranoia that death could be just around the corner.
== Background Information ==
== References == * {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix II|page=72-73}}
{{scroll|<references />}}
